  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Louisville (UofL) is a public research university in Louisville, Kentucky, USA, and part of the Kentucky State University system. Founded in 1798, it is one of the earliest city-owned public universities in the United States.</p><p>It offers undergraduate, graduate, and professional degrees in areas like engineering, business, arts, medicine, law, and public health.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>UofL offers a fun-filled student life, as you can join many of the 400+ student organisations, including cultural clubs, academic groups, and service organisations. Plus, you also have dedicated teams to assist with academic support, career advice, and more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>UofL offers multiple on-campus housing options, including residence halls, apartments, and suite-style living options. UofL has 11 residence halls and affiliated apartments. There are also Living-Learning Communities (LLCs) and Themed Communities (TCs).</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The major libraries include the William F. Ekstrom Library, the Kornhauser Health Sciences Library, and the Bridwell Art Library.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>The university has modern recreation centres, fitness zones, and athletic fields for competitive sports.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>The J.B. Speed School of Engineering boasts advanced labs and a new Student Success &amp; Research Building for engineering and STEM work.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>UofL has multiple dining halls and retail food locations across the Belknap Campus, along with meal plan options. You can also choose from well-known brands and cafes on campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
